From thorpej@nas.nasa.gov  Sun Dec 14 12:36:43 1997
From: Jason Thorpe <thorpej@nas.nasa.gov>
To: perry@piermont.com
Date: Sun, 14 Dec 1997 12:36:43 +0000
Subject: Re: getting to the floppy on a Multia

On Sat, 13 Dec 1997 18:49:48 -0500 
 "Perry E. Metzger" <perry@piermont.com> wrote:

 > The problem, if I'm correct, is merely one of busifying the i386
 > floppy driver (someone correct me if I'm wrong...)

Been there, done that :-)

The problem is that the IDE and floppy controllers have port overlap.
The Alpha IDE driver is bus'ified.  So, if you use the floppy, either
the floppy or the IDE will chose to "not configure" because of resource
contention.

Also, you have to take the i386 NVRAM dependencies out of the driver.

The former is the harder problem.

